Show no cursor at startup until a client sets one or the pointer moves

Hyprland shows its own cursor as soon as it starts. Where a monitor still
shows the boot splash's last frame (misc:startup_hold_layer), that cursor
appears over it before the session's cover has set the pointer's, on
Snapdragon X2 laptops as a black square.

cursor:hide_at_startup (false by default): from startup, no cursor is shown
until the client under the pointer sets one or the pointer moves. Once
shown, it is never hidden this way again.

Not yet upstream.

